      "writtenOn": "2025-07-30T01:31:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I suppose a third requirement I had written down is \"the parameter names in the .h file make sense to a reader\". Why would they be called x_in, y_in for ComposeToInternal but x, y for all the other functions?\n\nSince it\u0027s a private internal function in this case, I\u0027m on board with renaming in the .h, but in general I think it\u0027s not always possible to, uh, have all three cakes.",
      "parentUuid": "854f2fff_f3653e2e",
      "revId": "998f0ee6f282b5e5439b0338056a5f475bd33a79",
      "serverId": "fca2d64a-0420-3532-b200-12848c95a47b"
    },
